# Input
```vue
<!-- should generate diagnostics -->
<template>
  <LinkList>
    <template slot><a /></template>
  </LinkList>
  <LinkList>
    <template slot="name"><a /></template>
  </LinkList>
  <LinkList>
    <template slot="name" slot-scope="{ item }"><a /></template>
  </LinkList>
  <LinkList>
    <template slot="f o o"><a /></template>
  </LinkList>
  <LinkList>
    <template :slot="slotName"><a /></template>
  </LinkList>
  <LinkList>
    <template v-bind:slot="slotName"><a /></template>
  </LinkList>
  <LinkList>
    <template :slot><a /></template>
  </LinkList>
  <LinkList>
    <a slot="name" />
  </LinkList>
  <LinkList>
    <a :slot="name" />
  </LinkList>
  <my-component>
    <div slot="header">Header</div>
  </my-component>
  <component :is="tag">
    <div slot="named">Content</div>
  </component>
  <some-component>
    <template v-if="condition">
      <template slot="some-slot">Nested</template>
    </template>
  </some-component>
</template>

```

# Diagnostics
```
invalid.vue:4:15 lint/nursery/noVueDeprecatedSlotAttribute ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

  × The slot attribute is deprecated.
  
    2 │ <template>
    3 │   <LinkList>
  > 4 │     <template slot><a /></template>
      │               ^^^^
    5 │   </LinkList>
    6 │   <LinkList>
  
  i Vue 3 treats it as a regular attribute, so the content goes to the component's default slot instead of the named slot.
  
  i Use the v-slot directive on a <template> element instead, for example <template v-slot:name> or <template #name>.
  
  i This rule belongs to the nursery group, which means it is not yet stable and may change in the future. Visit https://biomejs.dev/linter/#nursery for more information.
  

```

